# Code quality

- Readable, predictable code beats cleverness; functions and components stay small.
- No magic numbers/strings—use named constants or enums when meaning matters.
- Flatten deep nesting; extract helpers when logic branches obscure intent.
- Comments explain **why**, not what the code already says.
- Avoid unnecessary casts, `any`, and giant files.
- Design for testability at boundaries (pure domain, services), not by mocking every child component.
